# A number followed by an unknown unit names the valid units.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where duration > 1x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..24
  PIPELINE@0..23
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..23
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..23
        NAME_REF@10..18
          IDENT@10..18 "duration"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        GT@19..20 ">"
        WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
        LITERAL@21..23
          TIMESPAN@21..23 "1x"
  WHITESPACE@23..24 "\n"

error[DS0003]: unknown timespan unit `x`
  --> query:1:23
  |
1 | t | where duration > 1x
  |                       ^ not a timespan unit
  |
  = help: valid units are `d`, `h`, `m` (minutes), `s`, `ms`, `us` (or `µs`) and `tick` (100 ns)
